60,3,1,talk,Minako,,Option A is a rota. Option B is a paid service. Option C is permanent assignments.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,Option C is dangerous. The previous tenants failed with it. Option A is rigid.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Sakura,,Option B sounds nice. Someone else cleans. I just have to be home?,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shizue,,Option B costs money. Option A costs time. Option C costs relationships.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Servas,,The firm's terms say we must tidy beforehand. That is a catch.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Minako,,"@Servas, the firm requires us to be in and tidy. That defeats the purpose of saving time.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minako, it does. But it is still less time than a full scrub. And it is consistent.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Sakura,,I don't want to tidy before the cleaner comes. That is extra work.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"The cost is 4,200 yen an hour. If we need two hours, that is 8,400 yen. Divided by five, that is 1,680 yen each.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Servas,,"That is less than the 2,300 yen we spend on supplies, and it saves us the labor.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Minako,,"I vote for B. It removes the time burden, even if we have to tidy.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,I vote for B. It is the most logical solution to the uneven usage problem.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Sakura,,I vote for B. I want the bathroom to be clean without me guessing.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"I vote for B. The cost is manageable, and it prevents the arguments over supplies.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Servas,,I vote for B. It preserves our relationships by removing the source of friction.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Minako,,It seems we are all in agreement.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,The data supports it.,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Sakura,,Yay! No more guessing!,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shizue,,I am glad we found a way forward.,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Servas,,A wise choice. Let us proceed.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
